{
  "diagnosis": "The counterexample reveals two core issues. First, when both push and pop occur in the same cycle (cycle 1), the current count logic incorrectly increments count for 2'b11, but should keep it unchanged (push=pop). Second, the s_ready assignment uses m_valid && m_ready without parentheses, causing operator-precedence ambiguity; it should explicitly group the simultaneous-transfer term. The count update must treat {push,pop}==2'b11 as hold, not increment.",
  "edits": [
    {
      "file": "rtl/packet_queue.sv",
      "start_line": 16,
      "end_line": 16,
      "replacement": "    assign s_ready = !rst && (count < DEPTH || (m_valid && m_ready));"
    },
    {
      "file": "rtl/packet_queue.sv",
      "start_line": 32,
      "end_line": 37,
      "replacement": "        case ({push,pop})\n            2'b10: count <= count + 1;\n            2'b01: count <= count - 1;\n            2'b11: count <= count;\n            default: count <= count;\n        endcase"
    }
  ]
}
